  tutorials:
  - specificTutorial: 1
    tutorialName: Welcome
    steps:
    - tutorialText: 'Welcome to [INSERT GAME NAME HERE] gameplay test! For this tutorial,
        we will go over just the basic information needed to play. Press [Next] now. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: You can go forward and backwards in these tutorial boxes, by
        pressing the [Back] and [Next] buttons. When you don't need to read any more,
        go to the last page, where the green [Got it!] replaces [Next]. Pressing
        [Got it!] removes the window.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'If you want to read the tutorials again, press the tutorial
        button top left, and all the relevant tutorials will be shown again. This
        button also works to view tutorials after [Do not show tutorials] is pressed. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'The basis of this game is to destroy the enemies approaching
        from above, before they can destroy you. The enemies vary in complexity and
        functionality, though there should only be simple enemies during this playtest. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: "To defeat the enemies, you will use cards as attacks and other
        useful features. How this works will we go over when we have enemies on the
        board and cards on your hand. \n\nPress the [Start Wave] button to start
        the game after this window is closed. "
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 2
    tutorialName: Drawing Cards
    steps: []
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 4
    tutorialName: Cards
    steps:
    - tutorialText: Please look at the rightmost card of your hand for further reference,
        as it is the least obscured.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: Cards! The cost of playing cards is displayed top left of the
        card. This is the cost in time, and everything is based on time.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: When time is progressed, enemy timers, enemy spawning, and enemy
        movement is also progressed by that amount. Don't worry, you also benefit
        from time passing (not yet), through items, cards, and progressing the map.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: Enemy movement is progressed with time, and is displayed top
        left in the interface. When the value on the right is reached, all enemies
        move. Most enemies move down, but some will try to move up.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'Top right of the card is it''s range. The ranges are: Anywhere,
        melee, projectile, maybe more. This restricts where you can play cards, and
        is usually balanced with more powerful cards to have the most restrictive
        ranges.'
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: '[Melee] is the lowest two rows, but can hit elsewhere.

        [Projectile]
        is the lowest row, but will fire upwards in a line.

        [Anywhere] is
        anywhere on the game board.'
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: Some cards do not have an effect on the board, and can be played
        even outside the board. These cards are described in the text box of the
        cards.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: Bottom right is tags. These are not functional in practice in
        this demo, but is generally used to alter cards during a run. You can safely
        ignore these.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: To use the cards, either drag and drop them, or click on the
        card and click where you want it to be used. Drop it into your hand again
        or click on the card again to cancel.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: Try to deal damage to the enemy with one of the cards now.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 5
    tutorialName: Enemies
    steps:
    - tutorialText: Ah, an enemy! You will have to defeat the enemies before they
        attack you.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: This is a melee unit, which can be seen on the overview when
        hovered. It is also not readying an attack immediately, which means it is
        not within range to attack. Melee units will try to attack when they can
        hit the two lowest rows and below.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: Underneath the enemy is their health bar. This enemy has a [Health
        Gate] as well. [Health Gates] negates damage past their position. Dealing
        4 damage to this enemy would only functionally deal 2 damage. Removing health
        down to a [Health Gate] removes the gate, and down to zero kills it.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: To the enemy's right, there is a timer. If the enemy can attack
        due to being in range, it will begin counting down, and at last, attack.
        Time is something that will be explained shortly!
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: When an enemy attacks, they will deal damage to other units on
        the board if blocked, and to you if not blocked. When you take damage, you
        will recieve a special card that represents damage added to your deck. If
        your entire hand is full of these cards, you lose.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: Let's deal with that enemy. Try to hover your cards, and I will
        explain the cards in detail.
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 6
    tutorialName: Damaging enemies
    steps:
    - tutorialText: 'Well done. Keep at it to the enemy dies. Remember to not deal
        too much damage into a [Health Gate]. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'Now kill it, prefferably before other enemies spawn. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 7
    tutorialName: Enemy is killed
    steps:
    - tutorialText: 'Awesome! Now you are pretty much free to continue playing this
        seed. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'There might be more tutorials popping up, but they should not
        be too long. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'Enemies are more likely to spawn if there are few enemies on
        the board at once. This mechanic will be reworked. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'There are no end to enemies now, and the only way out of the
        game is ALT + F4. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'Forgor to mention: To draw more cards, press the draw cards
        button. Doing so costs 3 time, but draws up to hand size. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'You can also discard cards by "using" them on the discard text
        down right. This will put it in the discard pile. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'You can also wait. It takes 1 time and does nothing. Waiting
        can be powerful, or plain stupid. '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    - tutorialText: 'Good luck :) '
      pointAt: {x: 0, y: 0}
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 8
    tutorialName: Enemy Info
    steps: []
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 9
    tutorialName: Enemy attacking
    steps: []
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  - specificTutorial: 10
    tutorialName: Damaged!
    steps: []
    currentStep: 0
    shown: 0
  tutorialSizes:
  - {x: 500, y: 300}
  - {x: 700, y: 450}
  - {x: 900, y: 600}
